            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0381" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg265"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/2303.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Hale to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 55]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my despatch No. 53 of January 8 I
                    transmitted a copy of the Foreign Office’s reply of January 5 to my note of
                    December 30. The Foreign Office note was not perspicuous, and I thought other
                    correspondence unnecessary. Upon reflection I changed my mind and have the honor
                    to enclose copy of my note of this date in reply.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. J. Hale.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d213-a1.xml" xpointer="d213-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
